\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{3}{The proposed earning-roles loop. Orange marks situated observation, green marks responsibility-safe evidence, and blue marks the future decision and its independently scored consequence. The feedback edge is delayed: it can change a later read cut but cannot rewrite a sealed assignment. Each artifact shown in the diagram is a planned ledger field, not a reported result}{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Evidence-to-role state. The episode lane records what the producer and recipient actually do; the public-evidence lane projects only typed, responsibility-checked fields; and the local-decision lane reads eligible rows at a read cut before sealing an assignment. Target outcomes arrive after the seal and update only the matching selected opportunity. The representation and updater remain replaceable interfaces.}}{3}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method-state}{{2}{3}{Evidence-to-role state. The episode lane records what the producer and recipient actually do; the public-evidence lane projects only typed, responsibility-checked fields; and the local-decision lane reads eligible rows at a read cut before sealing an assignment. Target outcomes arrive after the seal and update only the matching selected opportunity. The representation and updater remain replaceable interfaces}{figure.caption.6}{}}
